      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"drkrash1969\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/eada6e/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> drkrash1969:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>If an effect says that, for instance, \"Heroes cannot play cards,\" the hero cannot play cards in the 1st phase of the turn - but can they draw a card instead? Or is it like that phase doesn't occur?Thanks.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The Draw phase, by default, allows a hero to draw a card. That's it. If you can't draw a card you don't get to do something else instead.</p>",
