      "created_at": "2013-01-21T06:23:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nielzabub\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/48/1986_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nielzabub:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The only time you couldn't draw an extra card from an effect is if you have to skip your turn. If you skip your entire turn, then you would not get a draw phase.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This also applies to effects that make you skip \"the rest of your turn\" before the draw phase, like Fanatic's Prayer of Desperation or Nightmist's Mist-Fueled Recovery.</p>",
