      "created_at": "2013-01-21T13:10:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>that wasn't the question. He means if he is forced to not play a card, can he draw an extra card by not using a power either.&nbsp;And the answer is yes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This clarifies it for me.&nbsp; But in doing so, it made me go back to the rules and realize I've been playing something wrong all this time: I was playing it that if you skipped playing a card, you could draw AND then if you didn't play a power, you could draw another card.&nbsp; Oops.</p>\n<p>Since no one else commented on the 1st question, I assume that the answer provided above is correct.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:26:12.557Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
